# Dark Terminal Protocol boot screen: boot.html as a Plymouth script.
#
# Lock stage: the lock screen's RobCo terminal (anerti.lock), typing itself out: OMARCHY
# (TM) TERMINAL PROTOCOL, the emblem drawn in from the top, the banner (versions,
# copyright, hostname), a rule, then "> ENTER PASSWORD:" echoing an asterisk per
# character, over > VERIFYING... or > ACCESS DENIED. Init stage: Vault Boy, the progress
# bar and INITIALIZING SYSTEM... until the session starts. Shutdown and reboot type the
# terminal without its prompt.
#
# Every piece is cut from the mockup rendered at 1920x1080 (tools/build-plymouth); the
# layout block below says where each one sat. Other screens get the same layout scaled
# around the centre. Template: plymouth/src/vault-tec.script.

# Generated by tools/build-plymouth: piece -> x, y, w, h on the 1920x1080 grid.
